WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.172 --> 00:00:14.315
"We have to find the dungeon!"

2
00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:15.355
Gliss exclaimed.

3
00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:17.876
"That's where my parents are being held!"

4
00:00:17.896 --> 00:00:20.317
"I know," Darb said calmly.

5
00:00:20.337 --> 00:00:23.478
"But there's no sense rushing into the dungeon on our own.

6
00:00:24.138 --> 00:00:27.099
We should find our friends first, and then look for it together.

7
00:00:27.479 --> 00:00:28.439
That was the plan."

8
00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:31.380
Gliss gritted her teeth, feeling frustrated.

9
00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:36.251
She and Darb had been arguing ever since she'd zapped them away ten minutes earlier.

10
00:00:36.271 --> 00:00:39.873
"Why are you being so unbelievably stubborn?"

11
00:00:40.194 --> 00:00:40.634
she cried.

12
00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:43.836
She was so exasperated that she poked him in the chest.

13
00:00:44.516 --> 00:00:48.379
To her surprise, Darb reached out and gave her a hard shove in return.

14
00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:53.322
"Hey!" she blurted out in surprise as she stumbled backward and onto the floor.

15
00:00:53.342 --> 00:00:57.105
"How dare you—" "Shh!"

16
00:00:57.625 --> 00:00:58.166
said Darb.

17
00:00:58.806 --> 00:01:01.248
Just then Gliss felt something whiz past her head.

18
00:01:02.184 --> 00:01:02.944
"Stay down!"

19
00:01:03.305 --> 00:01:05.906
Darb cried, flinging himself to the floor beside her.

20
00:01:05.926 --> 00:01:10.508
Thud! Gliss heard the thing hit the wall at the end of the hallway.

21
00:01:11.489 --> 00:01:15.111
Then she ducked her head as another whizzing object shot over them.

22
00:01:15.131 --> 00:01:17.152
"What was that?"

23
00:01:17.532 --> 00:01:17.972
she yelped.

24
00:01:17.992 --> 00:01:20.054
"Is someone shooting arrows at us?"

25
00:01:20.074 --> 00:01:22.395
"I don't think they're arrows!"

26
00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.416
Darb pointed toward the end of the hall.

27
00:01:25.136 --> 00:01:27.698
Gliss saw a long, narrow creature hanging there.

28
00:01:28.478 --> 00:01:31.700
It looked like some kind of lizard with suction cups for feet.

29
00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:37.264
As she watched, it pulled its snout out from the stone wall, revealing a sharp blade.

30
00:01:38.305 --> 00:01:41.768
Pushing off with its feet, the lizard hurled itself straight at them again.

31
00:01:41.788 --> 00:01:45.972
"Ah!" Gliss cried, rolling to the side just in time.

32
00:01:45.992 --> 00:01:49.054
"Sorry I shoved you," Darb said breathlessly.

33
00:01:49.074 --> 00:01:53.698
"There was no time to—" Three more of the creatures sailed past them.

34
00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:55.740
"I know," Gliss said.

35
00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.402
"And now it's my turn to save you."

36
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:00.024
She grabbed his hand.

37
00:02:05.252 --> 00:02:10.434
"Zap!" Zann grasped his grandfather's hands through the bars, feeling happier than he had in days.

38
00:02:10.454 --> 00:02:12.855
"Are you sure you're okay?"

39
00:02:13.195 --> 00:02:13.635
he asked.

40
00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:17.837
Boz chuckled, squeezing Zann's hands.

41
00:02:17.857 --> 00:02:20.618
"I'm fine," he said.

42
00:02:20.638 --> 00:02:26.141
"Luckily, I haven't been a victim of Morb's leech treatment for a couple of days."

43
00:02:26.161 --> 00:02:29.722
"Nor have I," said Teplo from the next cell.

44
00:02:29.742 --> 00:02:34.104
"I'm starting to think Morb ran out of those nasty creatures."

45
00:02:34.484 --> 00:02:37.066
Zann was happy to hear that Boz and Teplo were okay.

46
00:02:37.186 --> 00:02:39.727
But some of the other Reds in the dungeon looked weak and ill.

47
00:02:40.427 --> 00:02:42.509
The king and queen were sharing a cell nearby.

48
00:02:43.189 --> 00:02:46.131
Both were slumped on the floor, pale and shaking.

49
00:02:46.931 --> 00:02:49.292
Zann also spotted several other familiar faces.

50
00:02:50.373 --> 00:02:53.194
The mayor of Swamp Bottom was a few cells from the king and queen.

51
00:02:53.955 --> 00:02:56.436
Gliss' parents were huddled together farther down the aisle.

52
00:02:57.197 --> 00:02:59.578
Some of Boz's other Magic Master friends were there too.

53
00:02:59.598 --> 00:03:02.920
"I've got to get you all out of here," Zann said.

54
00:03:03.648 --> 00:03:04.629
He glanced at Teplo.

55
00:03:04.649 --> 00:03:10.334
"Fala is here—some other people too—and everyone is ready to fight Morb."

56
00:03:10.354 --> 00:03:14.297
"Ah, you've raised a brave boy, Boz!"

57
00:03:14.597 --> 00:03:15.778
Teplo said with a smile.

58
00:03:16.559 --> 00:03:20.942
Zann rubbed his hands together and pointed at the huge metal lock on Boz's cell door.

59
00:03:20.962 --> 00:03:22.924
"Open," he said.

60
00:03:23.324 --> 00:03:23.945
Nothing happened.

61
00:03:23.965 --> 00:03:26.987
"Don't bother, Zann," Boz said.

62
00:03:27.007 --> 00:03:31.050
"Morb has put a Dousing spell over the entire dungeon."

63
00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:34.353
"That's right," Teplo added wryly.

64
00:03:34.373 --> 00:03:37.494
"Do you think we would have stuck around if we'd had a choice?"

65
00:03:38.254 --> 00:03:39.535
Zann's shoulders slumped.

66
00:03:40.155 --> 00:03:43.436
He'd just regained his magic, and now it was useless again.

67
00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:48.838
"Without magic, how am I supposed to His words trailed off.

68
00:03:49.659 --> 00:03:55.181
He could almost hear Darb's voice in his head: It is possible to get into a house without

69
00:03:55.281 --> 00:03:56.101
magic, you know!

70
00:03:56.962 --> 00:03:57.642
Zann grinned.

71
00:03:58.362 --> 00:04:02.504
Any door that could be opened with magic could also be opened without it.

72
00:04:03.628 --> 00:04:06.869
He stepped away from the cells and scanned the walls near the steps.

73
00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:11.371
The item he needed should be here somewhere "Aha!"

74
00:04:11.731 --> 00:04:12.212
said Zann.

75
00:04:12.872 --> 00:04:15.713
He reached over and grabbed a key off a hook on the wall.

76
00:04:16.433 --> 00:04:19.575
It was inside the stairwell, just out of sight of the prisoners.

77
00:04:20.315 --> 00:04:22.116
Boz's eyes widened when he saw it.

78
00:04:22.136 --> 00:04:24.457
"Good thinking, my boy!

79
00:04:25.157 --> 00:04:26.938
Now hurry and get us out of here!"

80
00:04:29.119 --> 00:04:32.360
Morb rubbed his fingers together and touched the talisman in his hand.

81
00:04:33.104 --> 00:04:37.786
Energy emanated from it and flowed through the air and into the talismans of the trolls standing in

82
00:04:37.826 --> 00:04:38.247
front of him.

83
00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:43.489
Morb hated to give up that magical energy, especially when he had so little left.

84
00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:49.512
But he couldn't risk leaving the palace without strong trolls to guard him—especially not now, when he was

85
00:04:49.652 --> 00:04:51.033
so close to victory.

86
00:04:51.053 --> 00:04:53.914
"Come with me," Morb ordered the trolls.

87
00:04:54.795 --> 00:04:56.996
They marched behind him as he walked through the palace.

88
00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:02.923
The blob Wyssa had brought last week was still guarding the entrance, but it shrank back respectfully as

89
00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:03.644
Morb passed.

90
00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:08.827
Morb strode across the square, ignoring the few citizens that were scurrying about.

91
00:05:09.647 --> 00:05:11.388
Soon he reached the riverbank.

92
00:05:11.408 --> 00:05:14.670
"I should find what I need here," he muttered.

93
00:05:15.371 --> 00:05:18.392
Rubbing his hands together, Morb focused on the river before him.

94
00:05:18.412 --> 00:05:21.434
"Levitate!" he intoned.

95
00:05:22.175 --> 00:05:23.896
Energy sizzled from Morb's hands.

96
00:05:24.736 --> 00:05:29.219
With a groan the entire riverbank rose, dripping water and dirt.

97
00:05:29.939 --> 00:05:34.021
Morb waved a hand, and the mass moved until it was directly over him.

98
00:05:34.882 --> 00:05:39.704
The trolls stepped back, staring fearfully up at the huge chunk of earth hanging overhead.

99
00:05:40.445 --> 00:05:46.388
Morb smiled as his sharp amber eyes spotted a small, gray shape wriggling out of the dirt above

100
00:05:46.428 --> 00:05:52.452
him. Just as he'd expected, the leeches had burrowed into the riverbank as soon as they'd felt his

101
00:05:52.512 --> 00:05:57.158
spell. Now they had burrowed straight through and were falling from the bottom.

102
00:05:57.939 --> 00:06:00.540
Morb reached out and caught the first leech as it fell.

103
00:06:01.301 --> 00:06:06.044
Then he turned away, ignoring the dozens of others that were raining down around him.

104
00:06:06.064 --> 00:06:08.706
"That's all," he told the trolls.

105
00:06:08.726 --> 00:06:10.026
"Let's go."
